Error [E0121]: `t` was consumed by `.join()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/task_double_join.jet:4:11
    |
  4 |     print(t.join() ?? 0)
    |           ^
 Why: After a value moves to another name, the old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Give away a copy instead (`~t`) where it moved
move site: source bytes 38..39; reuse site: source bytes 63..64; consuming callee: .join()
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
